      "title": "Reject raw strings for enum-valued market fields",
      "description": "`TimeMeaning` is a `StrEnum`, so `\"period_start\"` compares equal to `TimeMeaning.PERIOD_START`. As a result, `Market(source_bar_stamping=\"period_start\", ...)` passes this validation but stores a plain `str` instead of the declared enum value. This bypasses the runtime validation applied to the other enum-valued fields and leaves the market object inconsistent with its type contract. Check that the value is a `TimeMeaning` member, and add a test that a matching raw string is rejected.",
